---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | ZoneOfWar"
  description="The terms that govern use of the ZoneOfWar website and drone cyber range platform."
>
  <Section containerClass="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-accent">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-text sm:text-4xl">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-faint">Last updated: 18 August 2026</p>

    <div class="prose-zow mt-8">
      <p>
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of www.zoneofwar.com, app.zoneofwar.com and
        the ZoneOfWar drone cyber range platform (together, the "Service"), operated by Siivix Oy
        ("ZoneOfWar", "we", "us"). By creating an account or using the Service, you agree to these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Eligibility and accounts</h2>
      <p>
        You must provide accurate information when creating an account and are responsible for activity under your
        account. Organization administrators are responsible for the conduct of users within their organization's
        workspace.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Authorized use only</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is intended for authorized cybersecurity education, research, product security and resilience
        testing. You agree to use missions, labs and any tools provided only within the isolated environments
        ZoneOfWar provides, and never to apply techniques learned on the platform against systems you do not own or
        are not explicitly authorized to test. See our <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a> and
        <a href="/company/responsible-use">Responsible Use principles</a> for details.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Subscriptions and payment</h2>
      <p>
        Paid plans are billed according to the plan selected at checkout or in your order form. Fees are
        non-refundable except as required by law or as otherwise stated in your order form. We may change pricing
        for future billing periods with reasonable notice.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        ZoneOfWar and its licensors own all rights in the Service, including mission content, scoring methodology and
        platform software. Subject to these Terms, we grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to
        access and use the Service for your internal training and evaluation purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Customer content</h2>
      <p>
        If your organization submits custom mission content, scenarios or data to the platform, you retain ownership
        of that content and grant us a license to host and process it solely to provide the Service to you.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to keep the Service available and reliable but do not guarantee uninterrupted access. We may modify,
        suspend or discontinue features of the Service, including specific missions, with reasonable notice where
        practical.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is provided "as is." Training outcomes, scores and skill validations reflect performance within
        ZoneOfWar's simulated environments and do not constitute a guarantee of real-world security outcomes,
        employment outcomes, or professional certification recognized by any third party unless explicitly stated.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, ZoneOfWar will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special or
        consequential damages arising from your use of the Service. Our total liability for any claim will not exceed
        the amount you paid us in the twelve months preceding the claim.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        You may stop using the Service at any time. We may suspend or terminate access for violation of these Terms,
        the Acceptable Use Policy, or applicable law, particularly any attempt to use ZoneOfWar training against
        systems without authorization.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
      <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of Finland, without regard to conflict-of-law principles.</p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these Terms: <a href="mailto:legal@zoneofwar.com">legal@zoneofwar.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
